      en: "The mechanical district of Bologna, often referred to as 'Packaging Valley,' is a world-leading center for the development and manufacture of packaging machinery. The roots of this cluster date back to the period following World War II, when a combination of technical ingenuity and entrepreneurial spirit transformed the Emilia-Romagna region. Bologna and its surroundings are home to hundreds of companies specializing in highly automated machines for the pharmaceutical, food, and cosmetic industries. Big names like IMA and Marchesini Group shape the landscape, supported by a dense network of smaller suppliers. The district is closely linked to the so-called 'Motor Valley,' as many technical innovations are shared between mechanical engineering and the automotive industry (Ducati, Lamborghini). Billions of euros in revenue are generated annually, with the vast majority achieved through exports to international markets. The region also benefits from close collaboration with the University of Bologna, the oldest university in the world.",
